{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bugfix: Table Ratio Calculation and Flexible Column Collapse\n\nProblem Description:\nWhen rendering tables with a mix of fixed-width columns and flexible ratio columns in constrained console widths (e.g. nested tables, or dashboards with Console(width=60) and expand=True), flexible ratio columns collapse to zero width, producing collapsed borders '||' with completely vanished column headers and cell values. \n\nAdditionally, rendering empty tables with expand=True in constrained widths or with zero ratios crashes with unhandled AssertionErrors (\"Sum of ratios must be > 0\") or ZeroDivisionErrors during ratio calculation.\n\nReproduction:\n```python\nconsole = Console(width=60, record=True)\ntable = Table(title=\"Worker Dashboard\", expand=True)\ntable.add_column(\"Service\", width=22)\ntable.add_column(\"Host\", width=18)\ntable.add_column(\"Load\", ratio=1)\ntable.add_row(\"Database Primary\", \"db-node-01.internal\", \"82%\")\n\nconsole.print(table)\nrendered = console.export_text()\n# Bug: 'Load' header and '82%' cell vanish completely into collapsed borders '||'\n```\n\nRequirements:\n1. Flexible ratio columns must maintain a viable minimum width (at least 1 character for content plus column padding) rather than collapsing to invisible 0-width columns with vanished headers and data.\n2. Ratio calculations and space distributions must gracefully handle edge cases (zero available space, negative remaining space, or all-zero ratios) without crashing with unhandled AssertionErrors or ZeroDivisionErrors.\n3. Existing unit tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794165802271}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Bugfix: Table Ratio Calculation and Flexible Column Collapse\n\nProblem Description:\nWhen rendering tables with a mix of fixed-width columns and flexible ratio columns in constrained console widths (e.g. nested tables, or dashboards with Console(width=60) and expand=True), flexible ratio columns collapse to zero width, producing collapsed borders '||' with completely vanished column headers and cell values. \n\nAdditionally, rendering empty tables with expand=True in constrained widths or with zero ratios crashes with unhandled AssertionErrors (\"Sum of ratios must be > 0\") or ZeroDivisionErrors during ratio calculation.\n\nReproduction:\n```python\nconsole = Console(width=60, record=True)\ntable = Table(title=\"Worker Dashboard\", expand=True)\ntable.add_column(\"Service\", width=22)\ntable.add_column(\"Host\", width=18)\ntable.add_column(\"Load\", ratio=1)\ntable.add_row(\"Database Primary\", \"db-node-01.internal\", \"82%\")\n\nconsole.print(table)\nrendered = console.export_text()\n# Bug: 'Load' header and '82%' cell vanish completely into collapsed borders '||'\n```\n\nRequirements:\n1. Flexible ratio columns must maintain a viable minimum width (at least 1 character for content plus column padding) rather than collapsing to invisible 0-width columns with vanished headers and data.\n2. Ratio calculations and space distributions must gracefully handle edge cases (zero available space, negative remaining space, or all-zero ratios) without crashing with unhandled AssertionErrors or ZeroDivisionErrors.\n3. Existing unit tests must continue to pass without regressions."}],"timestamp":1794165802271}}
